IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`

-- Stamp Duty Act 1978 (NT) -- duty on a motor vehicle certificate of registration. SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE: the rules are in
-- the Act's own actors and terms ("the applicant for registration", "the transferor", "the Registrar", "the
-- Commissioner"). The applicant's questions are in sda-seat.l4.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. This is not an official version of the Stamp Duty Act 1978. Copyright in Northern Territory legislation
-- is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted from reprint REPS013, as in force at 1 July 2025, deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/Stamp-Duty-Act-1978-NT-current-reprint-REPS013.txt, under the Northern Territory
-- copyright policy of 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 Oct 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 57(1) (pay the duty to the Registrar before the certificate is issued, 50 penalty units) with
-- s 58(1); s 59(1), (1A) (dutiable value, GST not deducted), (2), (3) (the transferor's 14-day notice of the
-- consideration) and (5) (50 penalty units), as regulative rules; s 59A (refund when the sale is cancelled);
-- s 61 and s 92A(3) (declaring an exemption); Schedule 1 cl 5 ($3 for every $100 or part); s 92A (the electric vehicle
-- concession, 1 July 2022 to 30 June 2027); Schedule 2 item 23(a), (b), (e), (j)(i), (j)(v) and (k) (exemptions an
-- individual meets).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 57(2) (hire vehicles), Schedule 2 item 23(c), (d), (f)-(i), (j)(ii)-(iv) and (l) (farmers, a change of
-- name, duplicates, the Territory, exempt entities, traders, research, event and enthusiast vehicles, error
-- corrections), and item 23(a)(iii) (a class "prescribed for the purposes of this subparagraph": no regulation is
-- deposited, so no class is treated as prescribed).
--
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Stamp Duty Act 1978 -- motor vehicle registration duty, seat-neutral core`

§§ `s 59(1), (1A) -- the dutiable value of a motor vehicle`

-- s 59(1): "dutiable value means: (a) in the case of the transfer of a motor vehicle by a sale and purchase at arm's
-- length -- the sum of the amount for which the motor vehicle and any additional equipment in or added to the motor
-- vehicle was sold (which is to include any deposit paid and any trade-in allowance) and the amount paid for dealer
-- delivery charges; or (b) in any other case -- the market value of the motor vehicle and the additional equipment ...
-- as at the date the transaction that gives rise to the application for registration of the motor vehicle is entered
-- into or at the date the application for registration is made, whichever is the greater." (1A): "calculated without any
-- deduction or discount for the amount of GST". "additional equipment" includes all equipment that is an integral part
-- of the vehicle or added before registration, including air conditioning. An "application for registration" includes
-- an application for the transfer of registration. Amounts are GST-inclusive.
DECLARE `Vehicle registration` HAS
    `the date the certificate is issued`                                                  IS A DATE
    `it is a transfer by a sale and purchase at arm's length`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount for which the vehicle and its additional equipment was sold`              IS A NUMBER
    `the dealer delivery charges paid`                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the market value with additional equipment when the transaction was entered into`    IS A NUMBER
    `the market value with additional equipment when the application is made`             IS A NUMBER
    `it is an electric motor vehicle`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `v` IS A `Vehicle registration`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dutiable value of the vehicle` MEANS
    IF `v`'s `it is a transfer by a sale and purchase at arm's length`
    THEN `v`'s `the amount for which the vehicle and its additional equipment was sold` PLUS `v`'s `the dealer delivery charges paid`
    ELSE `the greater of` (`v`'s `the market value with additional equipment when the transaction was entered into`)
                          (`v`'s `the market value with additional equipment when the application is made`)

§§ `Schedule 1 cl 5 -- $3 for every $100 or part`

-- Schedule 1 cl 5: "(1) A motor vehicle certificate of registration is a dutiable instrument. (2) The duty payable on a
-- motor vehicle certificate of registration is $3 for every $100 or fractional part of $100 of the dutiable value of the
-- motor vehicle." As for conveyances, the scale is applied only to certificates issued on or after 1 July 2017, when
-- Schedule 1 was last amended (No. 13, 2017).
GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule 1 cl 5 duty on` MEANS
    3 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` `the dutiable value`

`the first day of the deposited vehicle scale` MEANS YMD 2017 7 1

§§ `s 92A -- the electric motor vehicle concession`

-- s 92A(1): applies to "the issue of a certificate of registration for an electric motor vehicle during the period
-- commencing on 1 July 2022 and ending on 30 June 2027". (2): "the first $50 000 of the dutiable value of the electric
-- motor vehicle is exempt from duty". (4): "the amount of the exemption that may be claimed under this section is limited
-- to a maximum of $1 500". (5): an electric motor vehicle "(a) uses an electric motor for propulsion, whether or not it is
-- also fitted with an internal combustion engine; and (b) takes and stores energy from an external source of
-- electricity; and (c) is not equipped with a fuel cell for converting hydrogen to electricity" (plug-in hybrids are in;
-- a FACT). At $3 per $100 the duty on the first $50 000 is exactly $1 500, so the cap only repeats it (NOTES.md).
`the first day of the s 92A window` MEANS YMD 2022 7 1
`the last day of the s 92A window` MEANS YMD 2027 6 30
`the s 92A exempt part of the dutiable value` MEANS 50000
`the s 92A cap` MEANS 1500

GIVEN `v` IS A `Vehicle registration`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 92A exemption` MEANS
    IF      `v`'s `it is an electric motor vehicle`
        AND `the day falls from` (`v`'s `the date the certificate is issued`) `to` `the first day of the s 92A window` `and` `the last day of the s 92A window`
    THEN `the lesser of` `the s 92A cap`
             (`the Schedule 1 cl 5 duty on` `dv` MINUS `the Schedule 1 cl 5 duty on` (`the greater of` 0 (`dv` MINUS `the s 92A exempt part of the dutiable value`)))
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `dv` MEANS `the dutiable value of the vehicle` `v`

§§ `Schedule 2 item 23 -- exemptions an individual meets`

-- Schedule 2 item 23: "Any of the following motor vehicle certificates of registration: (a) a motor vehicle certificate
-- of registration issued to the person in whose name the vehicle was last registered before it was issued (whether
-- registered in the Territory or elsewhere and whether or not that registration has expired) other than: (ii) ... a
-- motor vehicle in which seating is provided for not less than 12 persons; and ... being registered ... by a person who
-- has, until so registering the motor vehicle, never paid any stamp duty in relation to that motor vehicle ...; or
-- (iii) [a prescribed class: none deposited]; (b) ... issued following a conveyance of the motor vehicle: (i) to a
-- person who is the spouse, parent, child or stepchild of the person in whose name the vehicle was last registered ...;
-- or (ii) to or from the spouse, parent, child or stepchild jointly with that person; if the conveyance is wholly by way
-- of gift; ... (e) ... issued to a person: (i) who is the executor or administrator of, or the person administering, the
-- estate of a deceased person for the purpose of transferring the vehicle to a person beneficially entitled to the
-- vehicle; or (ii) ... for the purpose of sale in the course of winding-up the estate ...; or (iii) who is beneficially
-- entitled to the vehicle under the estate of a deceased person; ... (j) ... in respect of a vehicle that is: (i) a
-- motorised wheelchair; ... (v) a trailer that has a gross vehicle mass of not more than 4.5 t [a caravan is a trailer];
-- (k) ... issued: (i) to a veteran who is eligible to receive a pension at the rate specified by section 22(4) or 24(4)
-- of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 (Cth); and (ii) in respect of a motor vehicle for the veteran's non-commercial
-- use". Whether a veteran is eligible at those rates is the Veterans' Entitlements Act's question: a FACT.
DECLARE `Vehicle exemption facts` HAS
    `it is issued to the person in whose name the vehicle was last registered`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `it seats 12 or more and the applicant has never paid stamp duty on it`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `it follows a gift to the spouse, parent, child or stepchild of the last registered owner, or jointly with them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is issued to the executor, administrator or a beneficiary of a deceased estate, for the estate`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the vehicle is a motorised wheelchair`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the vehicle is a trailer or caravan`                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trailer's gross vehicle mass, in tonnes`                                                       IS A NUMBER
    `it is issued to a veteran eligible for a pension at the VEA s 22(4) or 24(4) rate`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the vehicle is for the veteran's non-commercial use`                                               IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Vehicle exemption` IS ONE OF
    `exempt: re-registration in the name of the person it was last registered to (item 23(a))`
    `exempt: a gift within the family (item 23(b))`
    `exempt: a deceased estate (item 23(e))`
    `exempt: a motorised wheelchair (item 23(j)(i))`
    `exempt: a trailer of not more than 4.5 t (item 23(j)(v))`
    `exempt: a veteran at the special or extreme disablement rate, non-commercial use (item 23(k))`
    `not exempt under the items encoded`

GIVEN `x` IS A `Vehicle exemption facts`
GIVETH A `Vehicle exemption`
`the item 23 exemption for` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF      `x`'s `it is issued to the person in whose name the vehicle was last registered`
            AND (NOT (`x`'s `it seats 12 or more and the applicant has never paid stamp duty on it`))
        THEN `exempt: re-registration in the name of the person it was last registered to (item 23(a))`
        IF `x`'s `it follows a gift to the spouse, parent, child or stepchild of the last registered owner, or jointly with them`
        THEN `exempt: a gift within the family (item 23(b))`
        IF `x`'s `it is issued to the executor, administrator or a beneficiary of a deceased estate, for the estate`
        THEN `exempt: a deceased estate (item 23(e))`
        IF `x`'s `the vehicle is a motorised wheelchair`
        THEN `exempt: a motorised wheelchair (item 23(j)(i))`
        IF `x`'s `the vehicle is a trailer or caravan` AND `x`'s `the trailer's gross vehicle mass, in tonnes` AT MOST 4.5
        THEN `exempt: a trailer of not more than 4.5 t (item 23(j)(v))`
        IF `x`'s `it is issued to a veteran eligible for a pension at the VEA s 22(4) or 24(4) rate` AND `x`'s `the vehicle is for the veteran's non-commercial use`
        THEN `exempt: a veteran at the special or extreme disablement rate, non-commercial use (item 23(k))`
        OTHERWISE `not exempt under the items encoded`

GIVEN `x` IS A `Vehicle exemption facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate is exempt under item 23` IF
    CONSIDER `the item 23 exemption for` `x`
    WHEN `not exempt under the items encoded` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 61: "A person claiming an exemption from paying duty on a motor vehicle certificate of registration shall, with his
-- application for registration, lodge with the Registrar a declaration stating the grounds on which the exemption is
-- claimed." s 92A(3): "Section 61 does not apply to this section."
DECLARE `Vehicle claim` IS ONE OF
    `an item 23 exemption`
    `the s 92A electric vehicle concession`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Vehicle claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a declaration of the grounds must be lodged with the application (s 61)` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `an item 23 exemption` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the s 92A electric vehicle concession` THEN FALSE

§§ `The duty on a certificate of registration`

GIVEN `v` IS A `Vehicle registration`
      `x` IS A `Vehicle exemption facts`
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the duty payable on the certificate of registration` MEANS
    IF (`v`'s `the date the certificate is issued`) `is before` `the first day of the deposited vehicle scale`
    THEN `not covered` `the conveyance or registration is dated before 1 July 2017, when Schedule 1 was last amended (No. 13, 2017); the scale in force before then is not in the deposited reprint`
    ELSE IF `the certificate is exempt under item 23` `x`
         THEN `the duty, in dollars, is` 0
         ELSE `the duty, in dollars, is`
                  (`the Schedule 1 cl 5 duty on` (`the dutiable value of the vehicle` `v`) MINUS `the s 92A exemption` `v`)

§§ `ss 57-59 -- paying before registration, and the transferor's notice (regulative)`

-- s 57(1): "If a certificate of registration for a motor vehicle is, on issue, liable to duty, the applicant for
-- registration of the motor vehicle must, before the issue of the certificate, pay to the Registrar an amount equal to
-- the duty payable on the certificate. Maximum penalty: 50 penalty units." s 58(1): the Registrar "shall not register a
-- motor vehicle" whose certificate is liable to duty unless the duty has been paid and the Registrar is satisfied it was
-- based on the dutiable value. Clock: days from the application; the certificate is to issue on the day given.
`the maximum penalty under ss 57(1) and 59(5), in penalty units` MEANS 50

GIVEN `the certificate is liable to duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days until the certificate is to be issued` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `s 57(1) -- pay the duty to the Registrar before the certificate is issued` IS
    IF `the certificate is liable to duty`
    THEN PARTY `the applicant for registration`
         MUST  `pay the Registrar the duty on the certificate`
         WITHIN `days until the certificate is to be issued`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant for registration` BECAUSE "s 57(1): the applicant must pay the duty to the Registrar before the certificate of registration is issued (maximum penalty 50 penalty units); s 58(1): the Registrar shall not register the vehicle until it is paid"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 59(3): "Where an application for registration relates to the transfer of a motor vehicle, within 14 days after the
-- date of the transfer, the transferor shall notify on the form of application or in another approved manner the
-- amount received as consideration for the transfer." (5): a person must not fail to comply with (2) or (3).
-- "Maximum penalty: 50 penalty units." Clock: days from the date of the transfer.
`the days for the transferor to notify the consideration` MEANS 14

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `s 59(3) -- the transferor must notify the consideration within 14 days after the transfer` IS
    PARTY `the transferor of the vehicle`
    MUST  `notify the amount received as consideration for the transfer`
    WITHIN `the days for the transferor to notify the consideration`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the transferor of the vehicle` BECAUSE "s 59(3), (5): the transferor must notify the amount received as consideration within 14 days after the date of the transfer; maximum penalty 50 penalty units"

§§ `s 59A -- refund when the sale is cancelled (regulative)`

-- s 59A: "The Commissioner must refund the amount of duty paid on a motor vehicle certificate of registration if the
-- Commissioner is satisfied that: (a) the transaction ... has been cancelled; and (b) the motor vehicle ... has been
-- returned to the person from whom it was purchased; and (c) all money refundable on the cancellation of the transaction
-- (other than the amount of duty paid) has been refunded to the person who purchased the vehicle." No period is stated.
GIVEN `the sale was cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vehicle was returned to the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the money refundable, other than the duty, was refunded to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle duty must be refunded under s 59A` IF
        `the sale was cancelled`
    AND `the vehicle was returned to the seller`
    AND `all the money refundable, other than the duty, was refunded to the buyer`

GIVEN `the sale was cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vehicle was returned to the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the money refundable, other than the duty, was refunded to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `s 59A -- the Commissioner must refund the vehicle duty when the sale is undone` IS
    IF `the vehicle duty must be refunded under s 59A` `the sale was cancelled` `the vehicle was returned to the seller` `all the money refundable, other than the duty, was refunded to the buyer`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST  `refund the duty paid`
    ELSE FULFILLED
